00:31:19,061 --> 00:31:28,891
They would come together on the big roundups and try to show off a little as to who was the best bronc rider, who was the best roper, who was the best cutter.

504
00:31:28,892 --> 00:31:30,820
Cowboys comparing their skills.

505
00:31:32,160 --> 00:31:37,732
As early as the 1930s, rodeo was organized into a professional sport.

506
00:31:37,733 --> 00:31:40,720
Since then, it's become big business.

507
00:31:40,721 --> 00:31:43,720
Today, the Professional Rodeo Cowboys Association

508
00:31:43,721 --> 00:31:45,720
is a multimillion-dollar sport

509
00:31:45,721 --> 00:31:48,720
with professional cowboys competing

510
00:31:48,721 --> 00:31:50,720
virtually coast-to-coast and border-to-border

511
00:31:50,721 --> 00:31:52,720
at major events.

512
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:57,720
Bull riding always draws the biggest crowds.

513
00:31:57,721 --> 00:31:59,720
I think bull riding was always considered

514
00:31:59,721 --> 00:32:02,720
the most popular from a fan standpoint of the rodeo events,

515
00:32:02,721 --> 00:32:05,720
simply from the danger involved and the drama.

516
00:32:05,721 --> 00:32:08,720
It is probably the truest extreme sport

517
00:32:08,721 --> 00:32:11,720
the truest extreme sport that there is out there.

518
00:32:14,020 --> 00:32:17,520
It's athlete against athlete in the bull riding.

519
00:32:17,521 --> 00:32:20,760
They need to be able to kick, spin, move quick.

520
00:32:20,761 --> 00:32:22,860
Basically, you see the same things in bulls

521
00:32:22,861 --> 00:32:24,500
as you do in regular athletes.

522
00:32:24,501 --> 00:32:27,180
They need to maintain that tip-top condition.

523
00:32:28,680 --> 00:32:30,540
But there's a lot of cowboy tech involved

524
00:32:30,541 --> 00:32:32,780
before the competition even begins.

525
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:36,880
In the early days of rodeo,

526
00:32:36,881 --> 00:32:40,120
selected in an unscientific fashion.

527
00:32:40,220 --> 00:32:41,880
If a rancher thought he had a tough bull,

528
00:32:41,980 --> 00:32:45,520
he'd simply enter it in the rodeo.

529
00:32:45,620 --> 00:32:47,520
Often, though, these ranch favorites

530
00:32:47,620 --> 00:32:50,220
failed to spin fast enough, kick high enough,

531
00:32:50,320 --> 00:32:51,620
and put on a good enough show.

532
00:32:54,740 --> 00:32:57,740
Now with a sport gaining unprecedented popularity,

533
00:32:57,840 --> 00:33:00,740
there's no room for this hit or miss method of selecting bulls.

534
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:11,880
In quest to give fans and riders the most buck for their buck,

535
00:33:11,881 --> 00:33:15,880
breeders are now trying to genetically select rodeo-ready

536
00:33:15,881 --> 00:33:16,880
bulls.

537
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:24,880
Companies like American Bucking Bull are gathering every bit of

538
00:33:24,881 --> 00:33:27,880
information possible about champion bulls in order to

539
00:33:27,881 --> 00:33:29,880
selectively mate them.

540
00:33:29,881 --> 00:33:33,880
The hope is that their offspring will become super bulls.

541
00:33:36,880 --> 00:33:40,880
When we track the ability of these bulls and their records

542
00:33:40,980 --> 00:33:43,880
throughout the years, then certain ones evolve and rise

543
00:33:43,980 --> 00:33:46,620
to the top, so to speak, as the ones that everybody wants to

544
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:48,220
have as a sire for their calf crop.

545
00:33:50,820 --> 00:33:53,460
With so much riding on breeding the perfect bucking

546
00:33:53,560 --> 00:33:56,540
bull, more and more breeders are turning to artificial

547
00:33:56,640 --> 00:33:58,540
insemination to assure quality control.

548
00:34:02,540 --> 00:34:06,040
Companies such as Great Plains Breeder Service collect semen

549
00:34:06,041 --> 00:34:09,040
to collect semen from the champion bulls.

550
00:34:12,040 --> 00:34:15,040
It's then frozen for later use.

551
00:34:17,040 --> 00:34:20,040
When we look at each sample under a microscope

552
00:34:20,041 --> 00:34:24,040
to determine the quality of the sample,

553
00:34:24,041 --> 00:34:27,040
it has to meet certain parameters in order to go ahead

554
00:34:27,041 --> 00:34:31,040
and process the semen through the freezing process

555
00:34:31,041 --> 00:34:34,040
and then store it in liquid nitrogen.

556
00:34:36,040 --> 00:34:39,940
Our goal is to have approximately 40 million live

557
00:34:40,040 --> 00:34:45,380
normal cells in a half milliliter of volume.

558
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:47,780
Bucking bull breeders can purchase the semen

559
00:34:47,880 --> 00:34:50,680
to impregnate their own stock.

560
00:34:50,780 --> 00:34:53,660
There's a popular belief that the bulls are made to buck

561
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:55,920
by the cinching of their genitals.

562
00:34:56,020 --> 00:34:58,160
We talked to insiders who denied this

563
00:34:58,260 --> 00:35:01,800
and challenged us to find the jerk who'd take that job.

564
00:35:01,900 --> 00:35:04,560
They say the bucking is triggered by the use of a strap

565
00:35:04,561 --> 00:35:07,560
that is cinched just tight enough around the bull's flank

566
00:35:07,660 --> 00:35:09,360
that the animal tries to kick it off

567
00:35:09,460 --> 00:35:10,860
while attempting to toss the rider.

568
00:35:15,540 --> 00:35:17,500
Early bucking tests on young bulls

569
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:20,240
are done using a specially designed mechanical dummy

570
00:35:20,340 --> 00:35:22,040
as the rider.

571
00:35:22,140 --> 00:35:23,920
This is the bucking bull dummy that we use

572
00:35:24,020 --> 00:35:25,340
to train our young bulls.

573
00:35:25,440 --> 00:35:29,560
It is basically just a weight to simulate a rider.

574
00:35:29,561 --> 00:35:34,560
It has a timer in it, run anywhere from two to ten seconds,

575
00:35:34,561 --> 00:35:37,560
depending on the length of time that you want the mechanism to

576
00:35:37,561 --> 00:35:39,560
stay on the back of the bull.

577
00:35:39,561 --> 00:35:42,560
It also has an automatic release controlled electronically,

578
00:35:42,561 --> 00:35:45,560
much like your garage door opener, that you can hit at any

579
00:35:45,561 --> 00:35:48,560
time, and it will release this mechanism from the back of the

580
00:35:48,561 --> 00:35:49,560
bull.

581
00:35:49,561 --> 00:35:52,560
Although the system doesn't guarantee that every bull will

582
00:35:52,561 --> 00:35:55,560
be a champion, it's raised the quality of competition bulls

583
00:35:55,561 --> 00:35:56,560
considerably.

584
00:35:56,561 --> 00:35:59,220
It's raised the quality of competition bulls considerably.

585
00:36:03,260 --> 00:36:05,360
For those of us who want our cowboy kicks

586
00:36:05,460 --> 00:36:07,940
but don't want to ride the real thing,

587
00:36:08,040 --> 00:36:10,440
there's the mechanical bucking bull.

588
00:36:10,540 --> 00:36:13,040
There's cowboy wannabes everywhere,

589
00:36:13,140 --> 00:36:16,180
somebody that wants to be challenged and have some fun

590
00:36:16,280 --> 00:36:18,420
and want to do the cowboy thing.

591
00:36:23,120 --> 00:36:26,560
The first mechanical bulls were built in late 60s

592
00:36:26,561 --> 00:36:28,060
probably early 70s.

593
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:31,400
And they had them in the bar as the old

594
00:36:31,401 --> 00:36:32,760
Gillies type machine.

595
00:36:34,260 --> 00:36:35,940
Mechanical bulls are more than just

596
00:36:35,941 --> 00:36:37,940
amusement rides at honky-tonk bars.

597
00:36:40,940 --> 00:36:43,840
They can also be used as practice machines.

598
00:36:43,841 --> 00:36:44,980
And that's no bull.

599
00:36:47,480 --> 00:36:49,920
There is a lot of bronc riders, I think,

600
00:36:49,921 --> 00:36:51,780
that practice on them, and bareback riders,

601
00:36:51,781 --> 00:36:52,760
and bull riders, too.

602
00:36:52,761 --> 00:36:57,760
At the Rock and Bee factory in Cheyenne, Oklahoma, the bulls

603
00:36:57,761 --> 00:36:59,760
are built almost from scratch.

604
00:36:59,761 --> 00:37:04,760
Most of the parts we make right here, from cutting out the steel

605
00:37:04,761 --> 00:37:08,760
for the base to what we call a trunk and building that.

606
00:37:08,761 --> 00:37:12,760
And then we go to the body where we put on the cowhide and the

607
00:37:12,761 --> 00:37:15,760
padding and the horns.

608
00:37:15,761 --> 00:37:20,760
A 220-volt electric motor generates about 2 horsepower for

609
00:37:20,761 --> 00:37:22,760
horsepower for every bull.

610
00:37:22,761 --> 00:37:25,760
This inner workings are mechanical bulls.

611
00:37:25,761 --> 00:37:29,760
We have our buck gear here that runs a buck for the bull to go up and down.

612
00:37:29,761 --> 00:37:31,760
You got your buck motor down here.

613
00:37:31,761 --> 00:37:35,760
This is of course variable speed, goes at different rates.

614
00:37:35,761 --> 00:37:41,760
You have also your springs which is regulated by the weight of the rider which when it moves one

615
00:37:41,761 --> 00:37:46,760
directly when it reverses you feel more like a real animal with these springs the way they work.

616
00:37:46,761 --> 00:37:49,760
Going around here we see your spin motor.

617
00:37:49,761 --> 00:37:54,760
Our spin gear, this will go in about 15 seconds.

618
00:37:54,761 --> 00:37:56,760
It'll go about 11 or 12 revolutions,

619
00:37:56,761 --> 00:37:58,760
or it can go a little bit faster.

620
00:37:58,761 --> 00:38:02,760
It can reverse on a dime, just cuts back really quick,

621
00:38:02,761 --> 00:38:04,760
and that's what makes it more realistic,

622
00:38:04,761 --> 00:38:06,760
like a real animal, a bull cutting back quick,

623
00:38:06,761 --> 00:38:08,760
a horse cutting back quick.

624
00:38:08,761 --> 00:38:12,760
So you can make it really feel a lot like a real animal.

625
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:16,760
The control allows for a wide spectrum

626
00:38:16,761 --> 00:38:18,760
of spins, bucks, and speed.

627
00:38:18,761 --> 00:38:22,760
to toss and turn riders just like on a real bull.

628
00:38:29,760 --> 00:38:35,760
Some riders request that an exact combination of spins and bucks be built into their rides.

629
00:38:36,760 --> 00:38:42,760
We set it where on the bucks it'll do a little over 80, maybe 84, 85, something like that on the spins.

630
00:38:42,761 --> 00:38:47,760
It's gonna be in the mid 40s, 46s, somewhere in that range.

631
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:55,760
We try to set it where it's not unrealistic.

632
00:38:55,761 --> 00:38:59,760
Like bull riding, some Western traditions never die.

633
00:38:59,761 --> 00:39:04,760
They only evolve. Today, everything from chuck

634
00:39:04,761 --> 00:39:11,760
wagons to horse trailers are getting a makeover.

635
00:39:11,761 --> 00:39:15,760
Bodacious, considered the world's most dangerous bull,

636
00:39:15,761 --> 00:39:19,360
was ridden for the full eight seconds only eight times

637
00:39:19,460 --> 00:39:21,960
in 135 attempts.

638
00:39:22,060 --> 00:39:26,200
He was so feared that he was retired in 1995

639
00:39:26,300 --> 00:39:28,200
to protect the riders.

640
00:39:28,300 --> 00:39:31,700
Cowboy Tech will return on Modern Marvels.

641
00:39:38,220 --> 00:39:41,720
We now return to Cowboy Tech on Modern Marvels.

642
00:39:45,760 --> 00:39:50,100
Today, prized livestock can be moved in air-conditioned splendor.

643
00:39:50,101 --> 00:39:52,760
It would make a Wild West cattle barren envious.

644
00:39:56,140 --> 00:39:59,600
But moving animals by wheel in the Old West took some doing.

645
00:40:01,380 --> 00:40:05,020
In the days before highways, the only option was rail transport.

646
00:40:06,840 --> 00:40:11,560
Cowboys developed methods for loading the animals on trains as safely and practically as possible.

647
00:40:11,561 --> 00:40:14,560
Special precautions were taken to keep them from slipping on

648
00:40:14,660 --> 00:40:18,560
the wooden floors of the livestock cars.

649
00:40:18,660 --> 00:40:20,560
Those railroad cars were heavily bedded.

650
00:40:20,660 --> 00:40:23,400
They put a lot of bedding in there, whether that was sand or

651
00:40:23,500 --> 00:40:25,500
sawdust or straw bedding.

652
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:30,520
And for traction, they'd have cleats nailed into the flooring

653
00:40:30,620 --> 00:40:33,520
so that the cattle and horses wouldn't slip around.

654
00:40:33,620 --> 00:40:37,120
The advent of the automobile and the horse trailer in the

655
00:40:37,220 --> 00:40:41,560
20th century made moving the animals much easier.

656
00:40:41,561 --> 00:40:45,860
The 20s and 30s is when you started to see cowboys hauling

657
00:40:45,960 --> 00:40:49,640
horses around in almost exclusively a homemade trailer

658
00:40:49,740 --> 00:40:51,100
of one kind or another.

659
00:40:51,200 --> 00:40:54,500
And over time, obviously, they got more and more sophisticated

660
00:40:54,600 --> 00:40:59,140
and trailer companies developed very fine trailers.

661
00:40:59,240 --> 00:41:02,380
Yet there were still some things left to be desired.

662
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:05,220
With the straight load trailer, where the horse is facing

663
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:08,220
straight into the front of the trailer, obviously, when it comes

664
00:41:08,221 --> 00:41:12,460
comes to a stop. What he has to stop with is his nose.

665
00:41:12,560 --> 00:41:15,860
I mean, he has to brace himself against the floor of the trailer.

666
00:41:15,960 --> 00:41:19,360
In the same way, then going forward, it's difficult for him

667
00:41:19,460 --> 00:41:21,760
to keep his footing in some cases.

668
00:41:25,180 --> 00:41:27,780
Today's trailer designers have factored in road travel

669
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:31,680
from an equine point of view and come up with a slant loading

670
00:41:31,780 --> 00:41:32,780
design.

671
00:41:32,781 --> 00:41:35,780
And that's good news for the horse.

672
00:41:35,781 --> 00:41:38,780
So the horse is riding at an angle going down the road

673
00:41:38,781 --> 00:41:40,780
rather than straight on.

674
00:41:40,781 --> 00:41:43,780
We discover that it gives them just a little more comfortable

675
00:41:43,781 --> 00:41:44,780
ride.

676
00:41:44,781 --> 00:41:46,780
It gives them a little more security in the way they stand.

677
00:41:46,781 --> 00:41:49,780
As they come to a stop, they can lean with a shoulder into the

678
00:41:49,781 --> 00:41:54,780
side of the trailer and creates less traumatic experience with

679
00:41:54,781 --> 00:41:58,780
the start, stops, and turns that go with traveling in a trailer

680
00:41:58,781 --> 00:41:59,780
or van.

681
00:42:02,780 --> 00:42:06,780
Another cowboy invention on wheels was the chuck wagon.

682
00:42:06,781 --> 00:42:09,780
From it, they were served their usual fare of beans, beef,

683
00:42:09,781 --> 00:42:11,780
biscuits, and coffee.

684
00:42:11,781 --> 00:42:14,780
The famous West Texas rancher Charles Goodnight

685
00:42:14,781 --> 00:42:18,780
was given credit for engineering the first chuck wagon,

686
00:42:18,781 --> 00:42:22,780
or a farm ranch wagon that would have a kitchen

687
00:42:22,781 --> 00:42:24,780
and a kitchen cupboard built on the back of it.

688
00:42:24,781 --> 00:42:27,780
What the situation was, he was sending out a trail cruise,

689
00:42:27,781 --> 00:42:31,780
moving large numbers ahead of cattle from one pasture to another,

690
00:42:31,781 --> 00:42:34,780
so they would take the kitchen literally out to the pasture

691
00:42:34,880 --> 00:42:36,680
or along on the trail drive.

692
00:42:38,880 --> 00:42:40,480
Modern versions of the chuck wagon

693
00:42:40,580 --> 00:42:43,220
are the amazing recreational vehicles and trailers

694
00:42:43,320 --> 00:42:45,920
driven by some of the top rodeo riders and cowboys.

695
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:53,640
If you're going to go out on the trail

696
00:42:53,740 --> 00:42:55,580
or if you're going to go to a horse show,

697
00:42:55,680 --> 00:42:57,540
it saves you a lot of money on hotel fees.

698
00:42:57,640 --> 00:43:00,680
You can just pull in, unhook.

699
00:43:00,681 --> 00:43:04,340
You can actually sleep in your trailer if you want to pull over and have lunch.

700
00:43:06,260 --> 00:43:09,740
Today's cowboys pack more than just food into their RVs and trailers.

701
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:13,000
The vehicles are one-stop supply shops.

702
00:43:13,460 --> 00:43:14,940
This is what we call our basement area.

703
00:43:15,860 --> 00:43:17,260
We actually use this for storage.

704
00:43:18,040 --> 00:43:19,940
We carry a lot of stuff in here.

705
00:43:20,020 --> 00:43:22,880
These are show pads for horse shows.

706
00:43:24,160 --> 00:43:26,680
And they're different colored, multicolored pads.

707
00:43:28,040 --> 00:43:30,660
It's like a home on the range with four wheels.

708
00:43:30,680 --> 00:43:32,480
This is Living Quarters.

709
00:43:32,580 --> 00:43:34,780
It has a queen-size bed.

710
00:43:34,880 --> 00:43:35,980
It's our TV.

711
00:43:36,080 --> 00:43:38,580
It has closet, two-burner stove, coffee maker

712
00:43:38,680 --> 00:43:40,320
so we can make our coffee in the morning.

713
00:43:40,420 --> 00:43:42,420
This futon actually makes into a bed.

714
00:43:42,520 --> 00:43:46,760
Here's our refrigerator, the commode, our sink, and our shower

715
00:43:46,860 --> 00:43:48,340
for when we take nice hot showers.

716
00:43:51,940 --> 00:43:55,380
Whether out on the road or on a bucking bull

717
00:43:55,480 --> 00:43:58,440
or in a fast draw contest, the cowboy

718
00:43:58,441 --> 00:44:00,900
The cowboy continues to loom large in our collective

719
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:03,380
consciousness.

720
00:44:03,480 --> 00:44:07,520
There's something about him that we just can't let go of.

721
00:44:07,620 --> 00:44:10,120
These cowboys make their own way,

722
00:44:10,220 --> 00:44:12,180
choose where they want to live and who they're going to work

723
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:13,180
for.

724
00:44:13,280 --> 00:44:17,920
All those combine, I think, to give them, hold some of the

725
00:44:18,020 --> 00:44:23,700
most endearing values, I think, that America tries to claim.

726
00:44:23,800 --> 00:44:25,760
The men who still work as cowboys

727
00:44:25,761 --> 00:44:30,160
have bought into the mythic way of life of their predecessors.

728
00:44:30,260 --> 00:44:32,560
Holding on to the traditions of the job

729
00:44:32,660 --> 00:44:34,960
while modern technology changes it

730
00:44:35,060 --> 00:44:37,700
is a challenge their Old West counterparts never faced.

731
00:44:40,800 --> 00:44:43,220
But just like the cowboys of old,

732
00:44:43,320 --> 00:44:46,320
these men are determined to keep seeing the world

733
00:44:46,420 --> 00:44:47,620
from on top of a horse.

